tage layout clearly to determine spatial relationships?**  \n   → **Yes.** Wide-angle shots (Frames 10–16, 28–30) provide a clear overhead or balcony view of the entire stage, showing the podium’s position relative to seated rows and the audience.\n\n4. **Where is the podium positioned relative to the people (left/right/center)?**  \n   → **Left side of the stage (from the audience’s perspective).**  \n   - In wide shots (e.g., Frame 10, 11, 28), the podium is clearly positioned on the **left side** of the stage (audience’s left).  \n   - The seated laureates and royal family are arranged to the **right** of the podium (audience’s right).  \n   - The podium is **not center stage** — it is distinctly offset to the left.\n\n5. **Is there a distinct podium structure?**  \n   → **Yes.** The podium is a solid, grey, rectangular structure with microphones and a gold emblem — unmistakably a lectern for speeches.\n\n6. **Are multiple people visible around the podium area?**  \n   → **Yes.**  \n   - In close-ups (Frames 20–27), the speaker is at the podium, with other dignitaries seated immediately to his right (audience’s right).  \n   - In wide shots, the podium is surrounded by seated laureates and officials, confirming its spatial relationship to multiple people.\n\n---\n\n### 📌 Conclusion:\n\nThe podium is consistently shown on the **left side of the stage** (from the audience’s perspective), with people seated and standing to its right and around it. The wide shots confirm this spatial relationship clearly.\n\n✅ Therefore, the answer **'3' (Left side of the stage)** is **correct**."}, {'batch_start': 30, 'batch_end': 60, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_1176.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_1177.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_1178.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/8QdE--Y-x7U/frames/frame_1179.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_proc